{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q is implicated in the regulation of H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through multiple mechanistic pathways. The drug is shown to target several enzymes, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, all of which are ultimately linked to the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. These targets suggest a potential role for Methyl Lucidenate Q in modulating the activity of this transporter, possibly through the inhibition of downstream metabolic pathways or by influencing the cellular environment that affects transporter function. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the regulation of metabolic intermediates that influence transporter activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared connection to the transporter supports a plausible but not yet fully understood mechanism of action.",
